{"timestamp": "2025-05-09T18:19:57.675033", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Initialize an empty list to store the actions\n  actions = []\n\n  # Get the recipe for the desired item from the cookbook\n  recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item]\n\n  # Iterate over the items in the recipe and their counts\n  for ingredient_index, count in recipe.items():\n    if isinstance(ingredient_index, str) and ingredient_index != \"_key\":\n      # If the item is a primitive resource or an environment entity (not _key), find its index\n      ingredient_name = env.world.cookbook.index.get(int(ingredient_index))\n      if ingredient_name == \"water\":\n        actions.append(4)  # Use water to craft the item\n      elif ingredient_name == \"stone\":\n        actions.extend([1] * count)  # Pick up and use stone as many times as needed\n      else:\n        for _ in range(count):\n          if env.world.non_grabbable_indices is not None and int(ingredient_index) in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n            actions.append(4)  # Use the item to craft the desired item, but only if it's not grabbable\n          else:\n            actions.append(1)  # Pick up and use the item as many times as needed\n    elif ingredient_index == \"_key\":\n      # If the key is used in the recipe, find its index\n      for _ in range(count):\n        if env.world.non_grabbable_indices is not None and int(ingredient_index) in env.world.non_grabbable_indices:\n          actions.append(4)  # Use the key to craft the desired item, but only if it's not grabbable\n        else:\n          actions.append(1)  # Pick up and use the key as many times as needed\n  return actions", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
