{"timestamp": "2025-05-09T23:57:55.914743", "function_name": "craft", "function_body": "  # Initialize the action sequence with the use action (index 4) to pick up stone and water\n  actions = [4]\n\n  # Get the recipe for the desired item from the environment's cookbook\n  goal_recipe = env.world.cookbook.recipes[item]\n  \n  # Iterate through each ingredient in the recipe\n  for ingredient, count in goal_recipe.items():\n    # Check if the ingredient is a primitive resource (found in primitives set)\n    if ingredient in env.world.primitives:\n      # Find the index of the primitive resource in the environment's cookbook\n      primitive_index = list(env.world.cookbook.recipes.keys()).index(ingredient)\n      # Add a pickup action for each required count of the primitive resource to the actions sequence\n      actions.extend([0] * count + [4])  # Move to the primitive, pick it up, and move back (assuming one space per step)\n    else:\n      # If the ingredient is not a primitive resource, recursively call craft_v2 for this ingredient\n      # Subtract one from the count since we already have one in our inventory due to the pickup action above\n      actions.extend(craft_v2(env, ingredient) * (count - 1))\n  \n  return actions", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
